{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "comments-api-collection",
    "name": "Comments API",
    "description": "Full collection for the Comments monorepo API (NestJS).\n\nBase URLs (Collection Variables):\n- `baseUrl`: `http://localhost:3001/api/v1` (Docker) or `http://localhost:4000/api/v1` (`npm run dev:api`)\n- `graphqlUrl`: `http://localhost:3001/graphql` (or `:4000/graphql`)\n- `wsUrl`: `http://localhost:3001` (or `:4000`)\n\nRecommended flow:\n1. GET /health -> verify database, graphql, websocket are `up`\n2. GET /captcha -> sets `captcha` httpOnly cookie and auto-saves `{{captcha_answer}}`\n3. POST /auth/signup or /auth/signin -> sets `access_token` + `refresh_token` httpOnly cookies\n4. POST /comments -> create root comment (multipart/form-data, allowed HTML: <a>, <code>, <i>, <strong>)\n5. GET /comments -> list roots (auto-saves `{{rootCommentId}}`)\n6. POST /comments/{{rootCommentId}}/vote -> toggle like (+1) / dislike (-1)\n7. POST /comments (with parentId={{rootCommentId}}) -> reply, then GET /comments/{{rootCommentId}}\n8. GET /comments/search?q={{searchQuery}} -> Elasticsearch search (with PostgreSQL ILIKE fallback)",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3001/api/v1",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "REST API base URL including version prefix (use :4000 when running npm run dev:api)"
    },
    {
      "key": "graphqlUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3001/graphql",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "GraphQL endpoint URL (use :4000/graphql when running npm run dev:api)"
    },
    {
      "key": "wsUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3001",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Socket.IO origin URL (use :4000 when running npm run dev:api)"
    },
    {
      "key": "access_token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "JWT access token (httpOnly cookie set automatically by signup/signin/refresh)."
    },
    {
      "key": "refresh_token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "JWT refresh token (httpOnly cookie set automatically by signup/signin/refresh)."
    },
    {
      "key": "captcha_cookie",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "HMAC captcha token (httpOnly cookie set automatically on GET /captcha)."
    },
    {
      "key": "captcha_answer",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "5-character captcha code parsed automatically from GET /captcha SVG (or entered manually)."
    },
    {
      "key": "signupEmail",
      "value": "test@example.com",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Email used for signup/signin"
    },
    {
      "key": "signupPassword",
      "value": "Password1!",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Password for signup/signin (min 6 chars)"
    },
    {
      "key": "signupFullName",
      "value": "TestUser",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Full name (letters + digits only, 2-100 chars)"
    },
    {
      "key": "signupHomepage",
      "value": "https://example.com",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Optional user homepage URL"
    },
    {
      "key": "rootCommentId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Root comment UUID - auto-saved after creating or listing comments"
    },
    {
      "key": "voteValue",
      "value": "1",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Vote value: 1 (upvote) or -1 (downvote)"
    },
    {
      "key": "searchQuery",
      "value": "world",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Search query for GET /comments/search and GQL searchComments"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health check",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('All dependencies are up', () => {",
                  "  const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(json.status).to.eql('ok');",
                  "  pm.expect(json.database).to.eql('up');",
                  "  pm.expect(json.graphql).to.eql('up');",
                  "  pm.expect(json.websocket).to.eql('up');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["health"]
            },
            "description": "Returns status of database, GraphQL, and WebSocket. HTTP 200 = ok, 503 = error."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
              "body": "{\"status\":\"ok\",\"database\":\"up\",\"graphql\":\"up\",\"websocket\":\"up\"}"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Captcha",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get captcha (SVG + cookie)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Content-Type is SVG', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('image/svg+xml');",
                  "});",
                  "const svg = pm.response.text();",
                  "const match = /letter-spacing=\"6\"[^>]*>([A-Z2-9]{5})</.exec(svg);",
                  "if (match && match[1]) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('captcha_answer', match[1]);",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('Captcha code extracted from SVG', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(match && match[1]).to.be.a('string').and.have.lengthOf(5);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/captcha",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["captcha"]
            },
            "description": "Returns an SVG captcha image and sets an httpOnly `captcha` cookie (HMAC token, 5 min TTL).\n\nThe test script automatically extracts the 5-char code into `{{captcha_answer}}`, and Postman stores the `captcha` cookie in its cookie jar."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 SVG + Set-Cookie",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "header": [
                { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "image/svg+xml" },
                {
                  "key": "Set-Cookie",
                  "value": "captcha=<hmac>; HttpOnly; Path=/; SameSite=Lax; Max-Age=300"
                }
              ],
              "body": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"180\" height=\"60\" viewBox=\"0 0 180 60\">...</svg>"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Sign Up",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('Body has status=success', () => {",
                  "  const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(json.status).to.eql('success');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"fullName\": \"{{signupFullName}}\",\n  \"email\": \"{{signupEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{signupPassword}}\",\n  \"homepage\": \"{{signupHomepage}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/signup",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "signup"]
            },
            "description": "Creates a new user account and sets httpOnly cookies:\n- `access_token` (JWT, 15 min)\n- `refresh_token` (JWT, 7 days)\n\nBody fields:\n- `fullName` — required, 2–100 chars\n- `email` — required, valid email, max 255 chars\n- `password` — required, min 6 chars\n- `homepage` — optional http(s) URL"
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "201 Created",
              "status": "Created",
              "code": 201,
              "header": [
                { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
                {
                  "key": "Set-Cookie",
                  "value": "access_token=<jwt>; HttpOnly; Path=/; SameSite=Lax | refresh_token=<jwt>; HttpOnly; Path=/; SameSite=Lax"
                }
              ],
              "body": "{\"status\":\"success\"}"
            },
            {
              "name": "409 Conflict (email taken)",
              "status": "Conflict",
              "code": 409,
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
              "body": "{\"statusCode\":409,\"message\":\"Email is already registered\"}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Sign In",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Body has status=success', () => {",
                  "  const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(json.status).to.eql('success');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{signupEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{signupPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/signin",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "signin"]
            },
            "description": "Validates email/password and sets httpOnly auth cookies (`access_token` + `refresh_token`)."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "header": [
                { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
                {
                  "key": "Set-Cookie",
                  "value": "access_token=<jwt>; HttpOnly; Path=/; SameSite=Lax | refresh_token=<jwt>; HttpOnly; Path=/; SameSite=Lax"
                }
              ],
              "body": "{\"status\":\"success\"}"
            },
            {
              "name": "401 Unauthorized",
              "status": "Unauthorized",
              "code": 401,
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
              "body": "{\"statusCode\":401,\"message\":\"Invalid credentials\"}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh tokens",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Body has status=success', () => {",
                  "  const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(json.status).to.eql('success');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "refresh"]
            },
            "description": "Uses the `refresh_token` httpOnly cookie to rotate both `access_token` and `refresh_token` cookies."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK - tokens rotated",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "header": [
                { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
                {
                  "key": "Set-Cookie",
                  "value": "access_token=<new-jwt>; HttpOnly; Path=/; SameSite=Lax | refresh_token=<new-jwt>; HttpOnly; Path=/; SameSite=Lax"
                }
              ],
              "body": "{\"status\":\"success\"}"
            },
            {
              "name": "401 Unauthorized (no/bad refresh cookie)",
              "status": "Unauthorized",
              "code": 401,
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
              "body": "{\"statusCode\":401,\"message\":\"Unauthorized\"}"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Comments",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get root comments (paginated)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Response has data array and pagination metadata', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(json).to.have.property('data');",
                  "  pm.expect(json.data).to.be.an('array');",
                  "  pm.expect(json).to.have.property('total');",
                  "  pm.expect(json).to.have.property('totalPages');",
                  "});",
                  "if (Array.isArray(json.data) && json.data.length > 0) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('rootCommentId', json.data[0].id);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/comments?page=1&limit=25&sort=createdAt&order=desc",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["comments"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "page", "value": "1", "description": "Page number (>=1, default: 1)" },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "25",
                  "description": "Items per page (1-25, default: 25)"
                },
                {
                  "key": "sort",
                  "value": "createdAt",
                  "description": "Sort field: createdAt | fullName | email"
                },
                { "key": "order", "value": "desc", "description": "Sort direction: asc | desc" }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns a paginated list of root-level comments.\n\nResponse: `{ data: CommentResponse[], total: number, totalPages: number, status: 'success', message: string }`."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
              "body": "{\n  \"data\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"uuid\",\n      \"text\": \"Hello <strong>world</strong>\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z\",\n      \"fullName\": \"TestUser\",\n      \"email\": \"test@example.com\",\n      \"homepage\": \"https://example.com\",\n      \"parentId\": null,\n      \"repliesCount\": 0,\n      \"votesScore\": 0,\n      \"userVote\": 0,\n      \"attachments\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"total\": 1,\n  \"totalPages\": 1,\n  \"status\": \"success\",\n  \"message\": \"Comments fetched successfully\"\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get children by root comment ID",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Response has data array', () => {",
                  "  const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(json.data).to.be.an('array');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/comments/{{rootCommentId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["comments", "{{rootCommentId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Returns all nested (child) comments for a given root comment UUID."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK - children list",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
              "body": "{\"data\":[],\"status\":\"success\",\"message\":\"Comments fetched successfully\"}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Create comment (text + allowed HTML)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
